"prosecutor | Wex | US Law | LII / Legal Information Institute (https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/prosecutor)\nciteturn23view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/prosecutor\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 28\nL0: Please help us improve our site!\nL1: \nL2: 【0†No thank you】\nL3: # prosecutor\nL4: A prosecutor is a lawyer who initiates 【1†prosecution】 of 【2†criminal offenses】, and presents the case for prosecution in a 【3†criminal proceeding】. The official name for the position of state prosecutors is district attorney.\nL5: For example, California Government Code § 26500 provides that “[t]he district attorney is the public prosecutor, except as otherwise provided by law [and] [t]he public prosecutor shall attend the courts, and within his or her discretion shall initiate and conduct on behalf of the people all prosecutions for public offenses.” At the federal level, the office of U.S. Attorney may serve as the prosecutor for federal crimes. The 【4†Office of the U.S. Attorneys describes†www.justice.gov】 U.S.\nL6: Attorneys as the “chief federal law enforcement officers in their district.”\nL7: [Last reviewed in November of 2020 by the 【5†Wex Definitions Team†about.law.cornell.edu】]\nL8: \nL9: Wex\nL10: \nL11:   * 【6†THE LEGAL PROCESS】\nL12:   * 【7†criminal law】\nL13:   * 【8†criminal procedure】\nL14:   * 【9†wex definitions】\nL15: ## Wex Toolbox\nL16: \nL17: * * *\nL18: \nL19: * * *\nL20: \nL21:   * 【10†Accessibility】\nL22:   * 【11†About LII】\nL23:   * 【12†Contact us】\nL24:   * 【13†Advertise here】\nL25:   * 【14†Help】\nL26:   * 【15†Terms of use】\nL27:   * 【16†Privacy】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn23view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/defense%20counsel\",\"lineno\":null}); \nURL https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/defense%20counsel is not accessible via this tool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nplaintiff | Wex | US Law | LII / Legal Information Institute (https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/plaintiff)\nciteturn23view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/plaintiff\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 33\nL0: Please help us improve our site!\nL1: \nL2: 【0†No thank you】\nL3: # plaintiff\nL4: \nL5: Plaintiff is the 【1†party】 who initiates a 【2†lawsuit】 in a 【3†civil case】 by 【4†filing】 a 【5†complaint】 against the 【6†defendant】 or, in some proceedings, the 【7†respondent】 (depending on the type of civil case). The plaintiff seeks a legal 【8†remedy】, such as 【9†damages】 or 【10†injunctive relief】, and bears the 【11†burden of proof】 to establish the 【12†claims】 made in the 【13†action】.\nL6: \nL7: See also: 【14†civil procedure】\nL8: [Last reviewed in September of 2025 by the 【15†Wex Definitions Team†about.law.cornell.edu】]\nL9: \nL10: Wex\nL11: \nL12:   * 【16†THE LEGAL PROCESS】\nL13:   * 【17†appellate procedure】\nL14:   * 【18†courts】\nL15:   * 【19†legal practice/ethics】\nL16:   * 【20†wex definitions】\nL17:   * 【21†civil procedure】\nL18:   * 【22†courts and procedure】\nL19:   * 【23†legal education and practice】\nL20: ## Wex Toolbox\nL21: \nL22: * * *\nL23: \nL24: * * *\nL25: \nL26:   * 【24†Accessibility】\nL27:   * 【25†About LII】\nL28:   * 【26†Contact us】\nL29:   * 【27†Advertise here】\nL30:   * 【28†Help】\nL31:   * 【29†Terms of use】\nL32:   * 【30†Privacy】\n"
